{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>To know</b> — The tav is superfluous, likewise לקחת, and likewise the lamed. The sense of the proverbs: let a person know wisdom, which is the root of everything, namely fear of YHWH, as it is said: The fear of YHWH is the beginning of wisdom, and discipline to keep His commandments. And some say: habit for the ordinary person, understanding to distinguish between one thing and another, so that he does not set darkness as light and light as darkness."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:40.963035327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}